Z||000000||Smokey||08-25-99||02:10 PM||||I'm brand new to this board, as a matter of fact, I just came across it. Since I was here i thought i would register and join in on all the fun :-)<p>I have a 1985 2m4. But i have a small problem. It has a hesitation below three grand. Once it gets passed there, it runs great. If i get on it from a dead stop when it is warm it just spits and sputters for a while and then takes off like a bat outa hell. Yet when its cold i have no problem at all. I have replaced the plugs, wires, cap, rotor, and the air filter. it sprays gas just fine, so i dont think i need a new fuel filter.<p>could it maybe be the O2 sensor?<br>or some other electronic device?<br>please reply with some suggestions<p>Smokey-*Team Fiero*<br>(Wrap your ass in fiberglass)
Z||000001||Patrick||08-25-99||02:45 PM||||<br>EGR system maybe?<p>By the way, I don't think there's a whole lot of fiberglass in a Fiero, if that's what you were referring to in your signature.<p><p> 
Z||000002||Smokey||08-25-99||03:13 PM||||The last thing i want to do is sound ignorant, but the body of a fiero is made out of a few different things. <p>RRIM- Glass Fiber reinforced reaction molded urethane (in other words, Fiberglass)<br>and TPO- thermoplastic olefin, to name a few<br>
Z||000003||Patrick||08-25-99||04:45 PM||||<br>Ok, fine...<p>
Z||000004||theogre||08-25-99||06:07 PM||||definatly check the EGR. look for anything else that might be leaking vacuum. Check the brake booster pipe from end to end.
